 "inference_time_or_retrain": {
  "weights": "UNCHANGED.  Every variant runs the pinned checkpoint's own tensors; a convolution at stride k*s is the same convolution evaluated at a subset of its positions, and the post-stem variants add no parameter at all.  No variant introduces a tensor.",
  "activation_ranges_measured": {
   "what": "the statistic an int8 rebuild would have to recalibrate, measured over 96 dev utterances on the float model",
   "encoder_output_absmax": {
    "T165": 7.4499,
    "T110": 7.4554,
    "T83": 7.3891
   },
   "prologue_kx_vx_absmax": {
    "T165": 17.0676,
    "T110": 16.9603,
    "T83": 17.2394
   },
   "verdict": "the ranges move by under 1 %, so the deployed scales carry over; this is the analogue of the max-|W| row surviving the vocabulary prune.  It is an ABSMAX over 96 utterances, and the extractor's policy is p99.9, so it indicates rather than proves that no recalibration is needed."
  },
  "what_it_DOES_need": "a re-extraction at the new shapes, of BOTH graphs: the encoder IR is built for one shape, and the decoder IR takes kx*/vx* as [1, T, 288] inputs, so T=83 changes its input tensors too.  That is a rebuild (the shape-ladder machinery already contemplated, ROCC_DECOUPLED s8.15.11), not a retrain.",
  "not_measured": "the int8 WER of any variant.  Everything in this file is the FLOAT model. On the one prior float-to-int8 comparison this workstream has (the lm_head prune, L300) the int8 delta was 1.4x-2.1x the float delta; that is an extrapolation from a different knob and is not quoted as a prediction.",
  "if_the_WER_must_be_recovered": {
   "lever": "QAT at the new stride",
   "script": "model_train.py",
   "price": "the long QAT run's own budget: 480 GPU-minutes on a TITAN RTX, 101,987 steps over 162.7 h of LibriSpeech train_big (model_pilot_qat_long.json)",
   "note": "this changes the schedule, not just the number, and it is a separate decision"
  }
 }
